sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch01-01> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Rules governing nature need not be those of traditional mathematics" ;
    dct:description "Although theoretical science requires that the systems it studies follow definite rules, those rules need not be the equation-based rules of traditional mathematics; the more general rules embodied in simple computer programs are equally candidates for describing the natural world." ;
    delphi:context "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 1, “The Foundations for a New Kind of Science”; section “An Outline of Basic Ideas” (from p. 1), p. 1. Scope: rules underlying natural systems studied by the exact sciences" ;
    dct:type "general-principle" .
}

